# End-to-end EMULATOR test: BIGTREETECH SKR Pico v1.0 (RP2040) under
# Renode in tick mode. Boots real firmware, completes identify +
# clocksync, brings up the full config (4 TMC2209s, 2 software-PWM
# heaters, 3 fans, endstops, 2 thermistors) and round-trips M114/M105.
# See "Per-printer tests" in test/emulator/README.md for the shared
# conventions.
#
# Ground specific to this board:
#   - TMC2209 multi-drop UART (four drivers sharing gpio9/gpio8,
#     distinguished by uart_address 0/2/1/3). Replies are always
#     master-addressed, so renode_hooks.sw_uart serves every address
#     from one register file; DUMP_TMC reads addr 0 and addr 3.
#   - test_klippy.py emits sw_uart for RP2040 "gpioN" pin names, and
#     sw_uart drives RX via the SIO GPIO_IN register (0xD0000004),
#     because RP2040 GPIO is a plain storeback region.
#   - rp2040_adc_stub.py: the local rp2040.repl leaves 0x4004C000
#     unmapped, so without the stub thermistor reads never complete.
#   - RP2040 keeps time with Timers.RP2040_Timer, a virtual-time model,
#     so (unlike the STM32F1 DWT) it needs no frequency pin under tick.
DICTIONARY rp2040.dict
CONFIG skr_pico.cfg
EMULATOR skr_pico.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
